    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0057" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg51"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/20356: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-16T15:00:00+02:00">March 16, 1942—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 16—2:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>218. Former Estonian Minister Varma<anchor n="71" xml:id="d52-f1"/> informed me
                    today that Germans about a month ago brought pressure to bear on Finns to secure
                    withdrawal of American Legation from Finland. Representations were made both to
                    Finnish Minister at Berlin<anchor n="72" xml:id="d52-f2"/> and to Foreign Office
                    here. Representations were oral and informal and Finns answered that severance
                    of relations with United States would cause unfortunate reaction among masses of
                    Finnish people and hence was not considered for present.</p>
                <p>Varma adds that Foreign Office officials now express regret Finnish Government
                    did not take stronger line in opposing German pressure <pb facs="0058" n="52"
                        xml:id="pg52"/> for breaking off relations with Britain last summer.
                        Gripenberg<anchor n="73" xml:id="d52-f3"/> lately Finnish Minister at London
                    has made his views on subject known here and both he and former Counselor of
                    Finnish Legation at London<anchor n="74" xml:id="d52-f4"/> have been frank in
                    deprecating wisdom of Finnish policy in relation to Britain. This Varma says has
                    had influence on Finnish Government’s attitude toward German pressure with
                    reference to United States apart from accepted fact that public opinion here is
                    definitely opposed to rupture with United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
